  "unresolvedAiThreads": [
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eBmQH",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3902168232,
      "path": "VAA.EAPI.GraphQL/VAA.EAPI.GraphQL.Domain.Account/Services/Under18AccountRequestFactory.cs",
      "line": 56,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3902168232",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`PhoneDetails` mapping can throw a `NullReferenceException` when the parent has no `ContactDetails` or `PhoneDetails` because `?.PhoneDetails?.Select(...)` can evaluate to null but `ToList()` is still invoked. Make the `ToList()` call null-safe so missing phone details produce an empty list instead of crashing the under-18 enrolment flow.",
      "decision": "invalid",
      "resolutionComment": "No code change. In C#, the null-conditional access in parent.ContactDetails?.PhoneDetails?.Select(...).ToList() short-circuits the remaining member-access chain when ContactDetails or PhoneDetails is null, and the existing ?? [] then supplies an empty list. ApplyManagedChildDetailsAsync_UsesConfiguredDummyEmailDomain and ApplyManagedChildDetailsAsync_UsesEmptyAddressList_WhenParentHasNoAddresses already execute this mapping with parent.ContactDetails unset, providing regression evidence that this path does not throw."
    }
  ],
